The old oak tree, it had seen it all. Generations of pups chasing squirrels in its shade, frisbee fights that ended in hilarious tumbles, all the biggest, most important moments of their lives, right here under its watchful eye. 

And this little Beagle pup? This pup, oh, this pup had the zoomies, the most epic, most pointlessly rambunctious zoomies the whole park had ever witnessed. You could follow the blur, a little brown streak of fur and wagging tail, for a good minute, maybe two, before they'd decide the best way to proceed was *this* way* and *this* way*. *Woof*! The *woof* of a thousand *woof*s*! It reverberated through the park, a *Woof WOOF* that *WOOF*ed a *WOOF* right in your *EARS*!

*Rrrrrrr...* the little dog's *Rrrrrrr...*}
